      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "body": "Seems fine, but I wonder if this is worth it to maintain. Would it not be easier to just use the runner image version as the key? E.g for the current image it would be `20260925.250.1`. I presume GHA will bump that every week or so, which seems fine to invalidate the cache this often, even if they only update paint.exe or so? Along with the vcpk.json hash, this should be sufficient?",
